        mfaUsed: Bool,
        deviceTrusted: Bool,
        emergencyLaunchRequested: Bool,
        approvalRequiredBudgetTier: Long,
    },
};
```

## Access-Control Requirement
The system manages advertising campaigns, creative submissions, and budget approval.

The people involved are advertisers, account managers, brand safety reviewers, and campaign directors. One person may hold both the account manager and campaign director role at the same time.

The resources are campaigns and creatives. Every campaign records its advertiser, who prepared it, its budget, its contingency, its budget tier, its risk labels, its scheduled start, and its status.

Every creative records its campaign, who submitted it, its risk rating, its content tags, and its status.

Each requester carries a reviewer level, and each request carries the current time, whether MFA was used, whether the device is trusted, and whether an emergency launch was requested.

A campaign director or account manager may approve a campaign budget only while the campaign is in review.

A campaign director or account manager must not approve a campaign budget when the campaign is not in review.

The review-status requirement applies when the campaign's budget tier is at or above the tier that requires this approval.

For campaigns below that budget tier, this review-status requirement does not block budget approval.

A campaign director or account manager may approve a campaign budget only when MFA was used.

When MFA was not used, neither a campaign director nor an account manager may approve the campaign budget.

A request by a campaign director to approve a budget that does not trip any prohibition above must be able to succeed.

