## Access-Control Requirement
This document describes how an advertising campaign system controls the approval of campaign budgets and the launch of campaigns.
The people involved are advertisers, account managers, brand safety reviewers, and campaign directors, and one person may act as both an account manager and a campaign director at the same time.
The resources are campaigns, which record their advertiser, who prepared them, budget, contingency, budget tier, risk labels, scheduled start, and status; and creatives, which record their campaign, who submitted them, risk rating, content tags, and status.
A campaign budget is first approved and then the campaign is launched on the same campaign, and the launch step can see the campaign's status and who prepared it.
When approving a budget, the account manager or campaign director who prepared a campaign may not be the one who approves its budget.
When launching a campaign, an account manager or campaign director may launch it only after its budget has been approved.
A campaign whose budget has not yet been approved may not be launched.
A run through the workflow by a campaign director that trips none of these restrictions must be able to succeed.

