## Access-Control Requirement
The system manages the review and merging of pull requests in a source-code repository.
The people involved are developers, reviewers, maintainers, and security leads. One person may hold both the developer and the reviewer role at the same time.
The resources are repositories, pull requests, and branches. Every pull request records its repository, its author, who approved it, its target branch, its approval count, and its status.
Each request carries the current time, whether the requester is on the VPN, and whether a break-glass emergency is in effect.
In this workflow a pull request is first reviewed and then merged, and the merge step can see the pull request's status and who approved it as recorded by the review step.
A reviewer or a maintainer may review a pull request only while it is open, and a request to review one that is closed or already merged is refused.
A maintainer may merge a pull request only after it has been approved, and a request to merge one that has not yet been approved is refused.
Neither a reviewer nor a maintainer may review a pull request that is no longer open.
A run through the workflow in which a reviewer reviews an open pull request and, once it is approved, a maintainer merges it, tripping no prohibition above, must be able to succeed.

