## Access-Control Requirement
This document sets out the access rules for the source-code repository access system.
The people involved are developers, reviewers, maintainers, and security leads, and one person may act as both a developer and a reviewer.
The resources are repositories, each recording its owner, team, sensitivity, whether the default branch is protected, topics, and status; pull requests, each recording their repository, author, who approved them, target branch, approval count, lines changed, whether a security review is required, and status; and branches, each recording their name and whether they are protected.
