The resources are cages, work orders, and access badges. Every cage records its tenant, zone-clearance level, authorized-occupant list, site zone, whether an escort is required, and status.

A facility tech, tenant engineer, or escort may enter a cage only when their clearance level meets or exceeds the cage's zone-clearance level.

A facility tech, tenant engineer, or escort whose clearance level is below the cage's zone-clearance level must not enter that cage.

A facility tech, tenant engineer, or escort may enter a cage only when they are on the cage's authorized-occupant list.

A facility tech, tenant engineer, or escort who is not on the cage's authorized-occupant list must not enter that cage.

A facility tech, tenant engineer, or escort may enter a cage only when they belong under the cage's site zone.

A facility tech, tenant engineer, or escort who does not belong under the cage's site zone must not enter that cage.

A request by a facility tech to enter a cage that does not trip any prohibition above must be able to succeed.

