The people involved are reviewers, program officers, grants officers, and applicants. One person may hold both the reviewer and program officer roles, or both the program officer and grants officer roles, at the same time.

The resources are applications and awards. Every application records its applicant, assigned reviewers, funding tier, requested amount, program code, and status.

Every award records its application, who approved it, who obligated it, its amount, its high risk flag, and its status.

Each requester carries the applications they are conflicted out of and their approval authority.

A reviewer who is the applicant for an application and is conflicted out of that application may not score it.

A reviewer who is not the applicant for an application is not blocked by this applicant-specific conflict rule.

The conflict rule applies when the requester is acting as a reviewer.

A requester who is not acting as a reviewer is not covered by this scoring restriction.

A reviewer must not score an application when they are both the applicant and conflicted out of it.

A request by a reviewer to score an application that does not trip any prohibition above must be able to succeed.

