## Access-Control Requirement
The system manages the authorization of grid switching orders and their field execution.

The people involved are planners, shift supervisors, operators, control room operators, and auditors. One person may hold both the planner and the shift supervisor role at the same time, and one person may hold both the operator and the control room operator role at the same time.

The resources are switching orders and lockout tags. Every switching order records its planner, its designated executor, its feeder, its voltage level, its circuit count, its status, its scheduled start, and its scheduled end. Every lockout tag records its order, who applied it, and its feeder.

Each request carries the current time, whether it comes from the SCADA control network, whether lockout-tagout has been verified, and whether an outage emergency has been declared.

A planner or a shift supervisor may authorize a switching order.

The field operator designated to execute an order may not be the one who authorizes it, keeping authorization and execution in two different hands, and a person who is not the designated executor may authorize it.

A switching order may be authorized only when the request originates from the SCADA control network, and a request from off that network is refused.

Neither a planner nor a shift supervisor may authorize a switching order they are themselves designated to execute.

A request by a planner, on the SCADA control network, to authorize a switching order they are not designated to execute must be able to succeed.

