An adjudication officer, supervisory officer, or background investigator whose clearance is not high enough must not view applicant data when they are not the assigned officer and the request is not from the government network.

When the requester is the officer assigned to the applicant record, the clearance requirement does not block the view.

When the request comes from the government network, the clearance requirement does not block the view.

A request by an adjudication officer to view applicant data without tripping any prohibition above must be able to succeed.

