## Access-Control Requirement
The system manages supplier invoices and their approval and payment in a finance department.

The people involved are clerks, approvers, finance managers, and auditors. One person may hold both the clerk and the approver role at the same time.

The resources are invoices and payments. Every invoice records its creator, its approver, its amount, its surcharge, its line item count, its status, its cost center, and when it was submitted; every payment records its invoice, issuer, and amount.

An approver or a finance manager may approve an invoice only after it has been submitted.

An approver or a finance manager must not approve an invoice that is still in draft status and has not yet been submitted.

An approver may approve a submitted invoice only when the invoice's cost center matches the approver's own cost center or is a division of it, such as approving an invoice for cost center "Sales" or for the prefixed sub-center "Sales-West".

An approver must not approve a submitted invoice whose cost center does not match or fall under the approver's own cost center, such as an approver from "Sales" trying to approve an invoice billed to "Engineering".

A clerk may create and submit an invoice.

A finance manager may issue a payment for an approved invoice.

An auditor may view the audit log.

A request by an approver to approve a submitted invoice whose cost center matches their own and that does not trip any prohibition above must be able to succeed.

