The people involved are contributors, reviewers, space admins, and readers. One person may hold both the contributor and the reviewer role at the same time.

The resources are pages and spaces. Every page records its author, reviewer, space, classification, whether external sharing is enabled, labels, and status, and every space records its members.

Each requester carries their clearance and space memberships, and each request carries whether it is on the corporate network, the current time, and whether emergency access is being used.

A space admin may enable external sharing only for a published page.

A space admin must not enable external sharing for a page that is not published.

A space admin may enable external sharing only when the page's classification is internal or lower.

A space admin must not enable external sharing for a page whose classification is above internal.

Only a space admin may enable external sharing for a page.

A contributor, reviewer, or reader who is not also a space admin must not enable external sharing for a page.

A request by a space admin to enable external sharing for a published page with internal-or-lower classification, tripping no prohibition above, must be able to succeed.

Write the Cedar policies now.

## Cedar Schema
```cedar
entity Role enum ["Contributor", "Reviewer", "SpaceAdmin", "Reader"];

entity User {
    roles: Set<Role>,
    clearance: String,
    memberships: Set<Space>,
};

entity Space {
    members: Set<User>,
};

entity Page {
    author: User,
    reviewer: User,
    space: Space,
    classification: String,
    externalSharingEnabled: Bool,
    labels: Set<String>,
    status: String,
};

action enableExternalSharing appliesTo {
    principal: [User],
    resource: [Page],
    context: {
        onCorporateNetwork: Bool,
        currentTime: datetime,
        emergencyAccess: Bool,
    },
};
```

