## Access-Control Requirement
The system manages automation and zone control for a smart office building.

The people involved are facility managers, zone controllers, maintenance technicians, and tenants. One person may hold both the facility manager and zone controller roles at the same time.

The resources are actuators, zones, and commission requests. Every actuator records its owner, its zone group, its device tags, whether it is flagged for maintenance, and its status. Every zone records its assigned controller, its criticality level, and its status. Every commission request records the device it concerns, who requested it, and its status.

Each request carries the current time, whether occupancy has been detected in the zone, whether the requester is on the building's on-site network, and whether a maintenance override has been declared.

A zone controller or facility manager may override a zone's schedule only when their control tier dominates that zone's criticality level, for example a Tier 1 controller overriding a critical zone or a Tier 2 controller overriding an elevated zone.

If the requester's control tier does not dominate the zone's criticality level, the schedule may not be overridden.

A zone controller or facility manager may override a zone's schedule only when they are that zone's assigned controller.

A zone controller who is not the assigned controller for a given zone may not override that zone's schedule, even if their control tier would otherwise dominate its criticality.

A zone controller or facility manager may override a zone's schedule only when occupancy is currently detected in that zone.

When occupancy has not been detected in the zone, the schedule may not be overridden even by that zone's assigned controller.

Neither a zone controller nor a facility manager may override a zone's schedule when they are not that zone's assigned controller, since assignment is required regardless of control tier or occupancy.

A maintenance technician may request a commission for an actuator, and a facility manager may approve that commission.

A request by a zone controller who is the assigned controller for a currently occupied zone, and whose control tier dominates that zone's criticality, to override its schedule must be able to succeed.

